---
alwaysApply: true
description: "commit style convention"
---

```
git commit -m "type: brief description

- Detailed bullet point 1
- Detailed bullet point 2
- Detailed bullet point 3

Changelog:
- file1.py: specific change description
- file2.py: another change description"
```

- Types: feat, fix, refactor, test, docs, chore
- English only for commit messages
- Detailed body with bullet points explaining changes
- Changelog section listing specific file changes
- Conventional commits format for automated versioning
